blem "Determine ${lim}_{x\\to (1,-2)}\\sqrt[3]{3x-2y+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\sqrt[3]{3x-2y+1}.\n$$\n\nThe function $f(x,y)$ is continuous for all values of $x$ and $y.$ So, we can calculate the limit by substituting $(1,-2)$ into the function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,-2)}\\sqrt[3]{3x-2y+1} & =\\sqrt[3]{3(1)-2(-2)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{3+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{8} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129329/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f2ac99b-55b2-5742-81ab-d2961db1250f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129329"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74909/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" :answer/id #uuid "c89eae4f-4ac1-5778-a888-5d5190d76a00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74909/selection/15aff851ab2807102904f6e00e765d26d734a91dd538d10b770cfeb2fdeede38" :answer/id #uuid "814041af-a211-5b1a-b088-c13740bfaafb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74909/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" :answer/id #uuid "43ed9952-fd65-58df-969c-41dde8d9943b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74909/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9ceb4528-b9d7-55ba-9c52-f3630e073f8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74909/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "17a06a4d-4e0a-55f7-96ce-4af0428c19e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74909/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3721c749-ba43-